{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Lq1br6T9HAHRkhqskMjHD","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# Deep repository review — 2026-07-22\n2:\n3:This is an as-found review of the live repository on branch\n4:`dualplan-routing-fix` at commit `6a752b4`. It covers code quality,\n5:architecture, requirements and prose, security, performance, tests,\n6:dependencies, configuration, CI, Git practices, licensing, accessibility, and\n7:internationalization readiness.\n8:\n9:Per the request, historical/log material was excluded from the review corpus:\n10:`docs/log.md`, `docs/archive/**`, `docs/iteration/**`, `docs/reviews/**`, and\n11:the owner-only `OWNER_SCRATCHPAD.md` were not audited. Generated OKF pages were\n12:checked through generator freshness rather than read one by one.\n13:`PROJECT_STATE.html` was assessed through its generator and a fresh 36-image\n14:width/theme/tab render matrix. Existing repository-review reports were used\n15:only as a regression baseline; their conclusions were not copied forward\n16:without re-verification.\n17:\n18:Ground truth at review time:\n19:\n20:- 728 tracked live-scope files; 58,445 Python lines across product scripts and\n21:  tests, including 30,064 lines in the 34 shipped scripts.\n22:- Full suite: **1,367 passed, 2 skipped in 275.66 s**.\n23:- Smoke tier: **1,079 passed, 2 skipped in 221.43 s**.\n24:- Ruff lint and format checks: clean. `compileall`: clean.\n25:- Strict trace: **SN=25, SR=109, LLR=97, TC=100**, with zero orphan,\n26:  integrity, schema, status, component, or interface findings.\n27:- Latest coverage data: **92% overall**, but with materially weaker individual\n28:  modules called out below.\n29:- Duplicate detector: green with its allowlist; without that allowlist it\n30:  reports **225 blocks across 101 allowlisted file pairs**.\n31:- Secrets/privacy repository sweep: clean. No private-key material was found.\n32:- Dashboard: 36/36 Playwright screenshots generated and representative light,\n33:  dark, desktop, and 390 px images inspected. No clipping, contrast, or\n34:  responsive-layout regression was visible.\n35:- `npm audit --package-lock-only`: zero known vulnerabilities. Playwright\n36:  1.61.1 is current. The compatible Ruff range already admits current\n37:  0.15.22; pytest intentionally remains on the constrained 8.x line while a\n38:  floating canary tests future majors.\n39:\n40:---\n41:\n42:## 1. Unfixed items and why\n43:\n44:The as-found report was committed before remediation as `4db2ba3`. The\n45:findings below intentionally continue to describe the repository at `6a752b4`;\n46:this section records what changed afterward and what remains.\n47:\n48:### Fixed in this pass\n49:\n50:- **H-1 — fixed.** `agent_session.py` now rejects prompt-in-argv when the\n51:  executable is, or resolves under the launch environment to, a Windows\n52:  `.cmd`/`.bat` shim. The guard runs during template construction and again at\n53:  the final process boundary. Stdin delivery remains allowed. Explicit-shim,\n54:  environment-resolved-shim, and safe-stdin regressions were added, and the\n55:  launcher/template/interface documentation no longer makes the false\n56:  “never through a shell” claim.\n57:- **M-1 — fixed in repository code and templates.** Both developer-workstation\n58:  scripts and both one-shot project setup scripts now require Python 3.11+.\n59:  Install modes refuse an existing older `.venv` instead of mutating it.\n60:  POSIX behavior and the PowerShell contract have regression coverage. The\n61:  existing local `.venv` is Python 3.9.6 and was deliberately not destroyed;\n62:  it remains a workstation cleanup item, not a committed repository defect.\n63:- **M-6 — fixed.** The live status/stack/session guidance now reports the\n64:  measured ~3.3-minute smoke and ~4.2-minute full-suite bars, gives the exact\n65:  documentation command, contains a genuinely forward-looking next action,\n66:  documents all six WI states, and no longer describes completed WI-226 as the\n67:  current owner of the complexity debt.\n68:- **Dashboard defects were registered, not silently buried.** WI-272 records\n69:  M-2 (status fidelity) and WI-273 records M-3 (semantic tabs), both as\n70:  `deferred` rows with live report anchors.\n71:- **Derived artifacts were regenerated.** The IF-041/IF-064 OKF pages and\n72:  `PROJECT_STATE.html` now match the edited registries.\n73:- **Budget-watched prose remained within its limits.** Before/after byte counts\n74:  were: `AGENTS.template.md` 9,975 → 9,975; `PROCESS.md` 60,420 → 60,420;\n75:  `PROCESS_OPTIONS.md` 161,007 → 160,980 (−27). No baseline restamp was needed.\n76:\n77:### Deferred, with reasons\n78:\n79:- **H-2 — core decomposition:** not safe as an opportunistic review cleanup.\n80:  The long coordinators combine state transitions and external effects; a","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1bda493d-d27c-440a-ba1f-31075a6a0204","uuid":"fbb92d4b-87d8-4738-8115-6207b55ae23d","timestamp":"2026-07-24T02:37:21.959Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"1:# Deep repository review — 2026-07-22\n2:\n3:This is an as-found review of the live repository on branch\n4:`dualplan-routing-fix` at commit `6a752b4`. It covers code quality,\n5:architecture, requirements and prose, security, performance, tests,\n6:dependencies, configuration, CI, Git practices, licensing, accessibility, and\n7:internationalization readiness.\n8:\n9:Per the request, historical/log material was excluded from the review corpus:\n10:`docs/log.md`, `docs/archive/**`, `docs/iteration/**`, `docs/reviews/**`, and\n11:the owner-only `OWNER_SCRATCHPAD.md` were not audited. Generated OKF pages were\n12:checked through generator freshness rather than read one by one.\n13:`PROJECT_STATE.html` was assessed through its generator and a fresh 36-image\n14:width/theme/tab render matrix. Existing repository-review reports were used\n15:only as a regression baseline; their conclusions were not copied